{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 11,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.671,
            0.049,
            0.846,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Finding the Unknown"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.846,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": "We have the expression 3k + 1 which gives the number of tiles needed to make an arrangement in Step k."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.127,
            0.847,
            0.167
          ],
          "content": "To check whether an arrangement is possible using 100 tiles at some Step k, we can solve the equation: $3k + 1 = 100$ . Find the value of k."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.176,
            0.847,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 8:** Madhubanti wants to organise a party. She decides to buy snacks for the party from the chaat shop in town. Each plate of snacks costs ₹25. The shop charges an additional fixed amount of ₹50 to deliver the snacks to Madhubanti’s house."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.253,
            0.848,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": "There are 5 members in Madhubanti’s family, including herself. Her parents tell her she can spend ₹500 on this party. How many friends can she invite to the party if she wants to give a plate of snacks to each person, including her family and friends?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.34,
            0.703,
            0.361
          ],
          "content": "Fatima’s method of solving this problem is shown below."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.365,
            0.671,
            0.386
          ],
          "content": "She represented the situation using a rough diagram."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.315,
            0.399,
            0.661,
            0.614
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_11_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.622,
            0.846,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": "Out of ₹500, if we subtract the fixed delivery charge, then Madhubanti is left with ₹450."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.66,
            0.847,
            0.698
          ],
          "content": "So the question becomes “How many plates of snacks, each costing ₹25, can be bought for ₹450?”."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.698,
            0.49,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": "The answer to this is $450 \\div 25 = 18.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.722,
            0.846,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": "18 plates of snacks can be bought for ₹450. Considering her 5 family members, she can invite $18 - 5 = 13$ friends to her party."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.807,
            0.933,
            0.845,
            0.95
          ],
          "content": "175"
        }
      ]
    }
